examples.question_text:
A rectangle has width $\frac{2x}{7}$ cm. Its length is three times its width. Write a simplified expression for its area.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\draw[draw=black] (0,0) rectangle (54,24);
\path (27,28) node[text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {length};
\path (57,12) node[anchor=west,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$\frac{2x}{7}$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Diagram not to scale.

examples.solution_text:
The length is three times the width.

$\begin{aligned}\text{length}&=3\times\frac{2x}{7}\\&=\frac{6x}{7}\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\draw[draw=black] (0,0) rectangle (54,24);
\path (27,28) node[text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$\frac{6x}{7}$ cm};
\path (57,12) node[anchor=west,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$\frac{2x}{7}$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Multiply length by width.

$\begin{aligned}\text{area}&=\frac{6x}{7}\times\frac{2x}{7}\\&=\frac{12x^2}{49}\text{ cm}^2\end{aligned}$
